-- title:
--   Relative dimension one for the Igusa scheme over ℤ_{(ℓ)}
-- statement:
--   Fix an integer $N \neq 0$ and a prime $\ell$, and write $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$ for the subring [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt ℓ`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) of $\mathbb{Q}$ consisting of those rationals whose denominator is coprime to $\ell$. Let [`ModularCurve.IgusaScheme N ℓ`](def/ModularCurve_IgusaScheme.html#L255) be the scheme obtained as the pushout of the two maps `fFin N ℓ` and `fInf N ℓ` out of `XMid N ℓ` (the two-chart gluing, over $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$, of the spectra of the chart algebras generated by `jFull N` and by its inverse inside the full modular function field of level $N$), and let `igusaTo N ℓ` be the structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} \mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$ obtained from the two algebra structure maps by the pushout universal property. Assume: `igusaTo N ℓ` is flat and locally of finite presentation; the underlying topological space of [`ModularCurve.IgusaScheme N ℓ`](def/ModularCurve_IgusaScheme.html#L255) is irreducible; for every point $y$ of $\operatorname{Spec} \mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$ the induced morphism from the fibre to the spectrum of the residue field at $y$ is smooth; and there is an open subscheme $V$ with nonempty underlying set such that the composite of the inclusion $V.\iota$ followed by `igusaTo N ℓ` is smooth of relative dimension $1$. Then `igusaTo N ℓ` itself is smooth of relative dimension $1$.
--
--   This is the assembly step for Igusa's theorem that the two-chart modular curve of level $N$ is smooth of relative dimension one over $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$, stated with its genuine inputs (flatness, local finite presentation, fibrewise smoothness over the two points of $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$, irreducibility, and the relative dimension at one place) left as hypotheses. It feeds the statement that the Igusa scheme is proper, smooth and geometrically integral.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_IgusaScheme_smoothOfRelativeDimension_one_igusaTo_of_smooth_fiber.lean

import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_IgusaScheme
import Definitions.Def_GaloisRep_Flat
import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.SmoothFiber

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

open CategoryTheory AlgebraicGeometry ModularCurve ModularCurve.IgusaScheme

theorem ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.smoothOfRelativeDimension_one_igusaTo_of_smooth_fiber
    (N : ℕ) [NeZero N] (ℓ : ℕ) [Fact ℓ.Prime]
    [Flat (igusaTo N ℓ)] [LocallyOfFinitePresentation (igusaTo N ℓ)]
    [IrreducibleSpace ↥(ModularCurve.IgusaScheme N ℓ)]
    (hfib : ∀ y : Spec (CommRingCat.of ↥(GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt ℓ)),
      Smooth ((igusaTo N ℓ).fiberToSpecResidueField y))
    (V : (ModularCurve.IgusaScheme N ℓ).Opens) (hV : (V : Set ↥(ModularCurve.IgusaScheme N ℓ)).Nonempty)
    [SmoothOfRelativeDimension 1 (V.ι ≫ igusaTo N ℓ)] :
    SmoothOfRelativeDimension 1 (igusaTo N ℓ) := by sorry
